-- Stack overflow is a runtime error in both backends: compiled code has no
-- stack check and faults on the guard region below the stack. `mod` keeps
-- the C compiler from turning the recursion into a loop with an
-- accumulator, which GCC does for `1 + 2 * _`.
count n = 1 + mod (count (n - 1)) 1000
main = print (count 2000000000)
